@page "/careers"
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Career Paths";
    ViewData["NoIndex"] = true;
}

<partial name="_SectionNav" model='"careers"' />

<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <span class="badge text-bg-secondary mb-2">Coming soon</span>
    <h1 class="h3">Career Paths</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Start from a profession — registered nurse, mechanical engineer, accountant, lawyer — and trace the path
        back: the programs that lead there and the courses along the way.
    </p>
    <p>
        Career Paths will also say plainly where licensure or program accreditation decides whether a route
        qualifies you, because a set of individually transferable courses is not always enough.
    </p>
    <p class="mb-4">
        In the meantime, most curriculum guides include a <strong>Career Pathways</strong> section describing the
        careers the course supports.
    </p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" asp-page="/Browse/Index">Browse courses</a>
</div>
